        "statement": "With $H,R$ as in Theorem~\\ref{thm:main}, for every $z\\in\\CC$,\n\\[\n |\\det(\\Id+zH)|\\leq\\det(\\Id+|z|R).\n\\]\nMoreover, $|\\det H|\\leq\\det R$ and\n$\\tr R-\\tr H=\\|A-B\\|_F^2$.\nEquality in all the one-sided inequalities\n$\\ee_k(\\lambda(H))\\leq\\ee_k(\\lambda(R))$, $1\\leq k\\leq n$,\nholds if and only if $A=B$.",
