        "scope": "in_scope",
        "statement": "Let $A,B,C$ be pairwise commuting positive semidefinite Hermitian matrices,\nand write $S=A+B+C$, $Q=A^2+B^2+C^2$, $F=6(A^3+B^3+C^3)+S^3$.\nThen $\\det F\\geq5^n\\det S\\det Q$.\nFor every $k$, the elementary symmetric functions of the singular values\nof $F$ dominate those of $5SQ$; also\n$\\ee_k(\\lambda(2F))\\geq\\ee_k(\\lambda(5SQ+5QS))$.",
